                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "A coder documenting a UTI sees in the Tabular under N39.0: \"Use additional code (B95-B97) to identify infectious agent.\" The provider documented \"UTI, E. coli.\" How should the coder sequence the codes?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "B96.20 (E. coli) first, then N39.0 (UTI) — organism is the etiology",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "N39.0 (UTI) first, then B96.20 (E. coli) — the additional code follows",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Only N39.0 — the organism doesn't need a separate code",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Only B96.20 — it captures both the organism and the infection",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "\"Use additional code\" means the main code (N39.0 UTI) is sequenced FIRST, with the additional code (B96.20 for E. coli as the unspecified cause of diseases classified elsewhere) sequenced AFTER. B96.20 cannot stand alone — its category description literally is \"as the cause of diseases classified elsewhere,\" which means it always supports a primary diagnosis code. The N39.0 + B96.20 combination correctly communicates UTI caused by E. coli.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Use Additional Code — sequencing</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"180\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"240\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">TABULAR INSTRUCTION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"290\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">N39.0 Urinary tract infection</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"325\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"22\">\"Use additional code (B95-B97)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"360\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"22\">to identify infectious agent\"</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"400\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">CORRECT SEQUENCE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">1. N39.0 — UTI</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">2. B96.20 — E. coli as cause</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"585\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Main code first, additional after</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"620\" width=\"940\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"675\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WHY B96.20 CAN'T BE FIRST</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"725\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">B95-B97 category description:</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"760\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"22\">\"as cause of diseases classified elsewhere\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Cannot be a principal diagnosis alone</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"840\" width=\"940\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"895\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">REMEMBER</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"945\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Use additional\" = main code first</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"985\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">\"Code first\" = etiology before this code</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Use Additional ≠ Code First — they're sequenced opposite ways"
                  }
                }
